><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/koopcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/koopcast.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="science" /><category term="trail" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Coach Jason Koop covers training, nutrition and recent happenings in the ultramarathon world.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Pace On Earth</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/pace-on-earth.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Pace On Earth" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/pace-on-earth</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/pace-on-earth.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="trail" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A Swedish ultrarunning podcast where the podcast hosts Ellen Westfelt and Johnny Hällneby talks about everything from cross training, nutrition, meditation, endurance sports and much much more.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Science Of Ultra</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-ultra.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Science Of Ultra" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-ultra</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-ultra.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[For endurance athletes who want to do more than improve race performance. The host, Shawn Bearden, hasn't published any episodes since October 2021, but the episodes are gold!]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Ultrarunning History</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/ultrarunning-history-podcast.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Ultrarunning History" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/ultrarunning-history-podcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/ultrarunning-history-podcast.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A podcast about the history of ultrarunning by ultrarunner and historian Davy Crocket.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Between Two Pines</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/between-two-pines.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Between Two Pines" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/between-two-pines</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/between-two-pines.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A running podcast for people who think running podcasts are stupid. Dom Grossman and Andy Pearson ask their guests hilariously insulting questions in a "between two ferns" style manner.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Way Of The Runner</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-way-of-the-runner.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Way Of The Runner" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-way-of-the-runner</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-way-of-the-runner.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Award-winning author Adharanand Finn talks to runners of every kind about the joy and experience of running.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Trail Runner Nation</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/trail-runner-nation.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Trail Runner Nation" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/trail-runner-nation</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/trail-runner-nation.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Trail Runner Nation is devoted to sharing knowledge and advice to the trail running community - from beginners to the pros! Tips and discussions regarding race nutrition, pacing strategy, mental focus and much more from well-respected members of the trail community.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Running long - A trail &amp;amp; ultra running talk</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/running-long-a-trail-ultra-running-talk.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Running long - A trail &amp;amp; ultra running talk" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/running-long-a-trail-ultra-running-talk</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/running-long-a-trail-ultra-running-talk.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="subultra" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="skyrunning" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Elite runner Francesco Puppi has conversations with key members of the trail & ultra running community from all over the world. From professional world class athletes to our Vert.run members and community.]]></summary></entry></feed>